## Still to do

### Phase 5 — scoring (this is the actual project)

The Lambda currently ignores the baseline table entirely. It needs to:

- Query DynamoDB for the identity's four facets
- Compare the event against each: unseen API, new region, off-hours,
  new source IP, no baseline at all
- Assign weights and sum into a composite score
- Only alert above a threshold, so two weak signals fire but one doesn't

Proposed weights: unseen API 3, new region 3, off-hours 2, new IP 2,
unknown identity 4. Threshold 5.

### Phase 7 — demo and writeup

- Plain-language explanations ("unusual because this user has no history of
  this API, at an unusual hour, from a new IP")
- MITRE ATT&CK technique ID on each detection
- Attack simulation runbook for the live demo
- Threshold tuning against normal team activity
- README with architecture diagram
- Verify `terraform destroy` rebuilds cleanly

